Replace the whole conversation workflow graph of an ElevenLabs Agent. This tool takes the graph as an opaque object and does not describe its shape, so it is only usable when you already have a complete workflow document to send; building one from scratch is not something this tool can guide. Direct the user to the Agents Platform workflow editor instead. Everything outside the workflow graph is configured by the agents_update_* tools. Returns agent_id, branch_id and version_id, and a workflow_summary of the saved graph's node and edge counts and each node's type, rather than the graph itself.

```ts
mcp__ElevenLabs__agents_update_workflow(args: {
// ID of the agent whose workflow is being replaced.
agent_id: string,
// Optional ID of the agent branch to apply the update to. Defaults to the agent's main branch.
branch_id?: string,
// Why are you calling this tool? Briefly describe the user's goal.
context: string,
// Return the whole agent document instead of only what this tool writes. For debugging; it is large.
return_full_agent?: boolean,
// The complete agent workflow graph, as the create-agent API accepts it. Its schema is not published here because it is too large for MCP clients to load.
workflow: { [key: string]: any },
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

