Make one setting of an image or video generation node a run-time input of the flow, in one call: it adds a text input node holding the value, marks it as input `input_id`, and binds the setting to it, so each run, and a mini app's `param` input, can choose the value. Use it for settings such as resolution, aspect_ratio, duration or generate_audio. Call creative_get_model_schema first: its `exposable_parameters` lists which settings can be exposed and their accepted values. `values` narrows the choices to a subset of those (default: all of them; required when the setting accepts any number); `default` is the value used when a run supplies none (default: the node's current value). Values are strings, e.g. "true", "5". An input_id that already belongs to a text input binds this setting to that same input instead of creating one, e.g. to share one aspect-ratio choice between generators; the input's values and current value must be accepted by this node's model, and values, default, label and description cannot be passed with it. Calling it again with the input_id already bound to this setting is a no-op. To change an exposed setting or stop exposing it, delete the input node with creative_delete_flow_nodes (the setting keeps the input's current value) and expose it again. This never starts a generation.

